{
  "report": "On October 8, 2026, City Wire corrected an earlier report stating Cedar United and Northbridge had agreed a transfer fee for striker Alex Stone. The correction notes the original claim was based on an unnamed source and that no formal offer, signed contract, or confirmed fee existed. City Wire withdrew any assertion of an agreed fee. On the same day, Club Bulletin reported that Cedar United’s spokesperson confirmed the club had not agreed a fee and made no formal offer, noting preliminary discussion with Stone’s agent on October 7, but declined to comment on pursuing a deal. No timeline or fee amount was provided. The correction and bulletin statements align: there is no confirmed transfer agreement, fee, or move. Alex Stone remains registered with Northbridge. All reports are based on statements from unnamed or limited sources; no independent verification or club confirmation of a fee or offer was provided."
}

{
  "report": "On Thursday, 8 October, Cedar United announced that goalkeeper Kim Park will miss the next league match on Sunday, 11 October, due to an ankle injury sustained during Tuesday’s training session. The club provided no return date or replacement goalkeeper. This follows a 2–1 victory over Vale City on Sunday, 4 October, where Park started and played the entire match, including the winning goal by Sam Lee in the 84th minute. Earlier on Monday, 5 October, the club appointed Jo Vale as head coach on a two-year contract, with the first training session scheduled for Tuesday, 6 October. Vale was not the head coach during Sunday’s victory over Vale City. No tactical changes or performance assessments were included in any reports."

}

